Hmm... having just last weekend ascended a knight, I suppose I could
offer a few suggestions. I started with extremely shitty stats
str:13 dex:8 con:11 int:9 wis:14 chr:17

After Excalibur, either an amulet of ESP or teh helmet of telepathy
are perhaps, your most neccessary items. Having such shitty hp's
makes it almost a neccessity to be able to see the monsters a few
moves ahead of time.
Then make yourself invisible (by whichever your prefered method is
(usually easy to find a way by the time you're down where you are))
and stealth (boots are easiest, or an elvin cloak.)
You have to be able to avoid monsters for a bit. I found that my
con went up on its own (due to practicing) and by the time I hit about
80 hp's, it was reasonably decent (though too late to help the hp's).
Pray for a nurse. Avoid the special levels, until you can get 'em up,
and use the #jump alot! You'd be amazed what you can do with a bit of
speed, alot of darts, and the jumping ability. =)

You'll never manage the quest with what you got (unless you find a wand
of death or some such)

Overall, knights are no wimpier then any other class that starts with
a low con, and they have it much better then those guys who are not
lawful, or have no longsword.

Dunno if any of this'll help, but if it does, your welcome. =)

